# Folded into /for-communities. A real 301 (rather than letting the SPA
# catch-all serve it and redirect client-side) is what tells crawlers the page
# moved, so the retired URL stops competing with the new one.
# Netlify matches top-down — these must stay above the /* rule to be reached.
/whatsapp-alternative      /for-communities   301!
/whatsapp-alternative/*    /for-communities   301!

/*                         /index.html        200
